{
  "title": "Popular AWS services, and how the lines are routed",
  "subtitle": "Each step shows one routing rule",
  "description": "Twenty-seven AWS services on a grid: an edge of CloudFront and WAF; API Gateway with Cognito; compute in Step Functions, Lambda and ECS; data in DynamoDB, ElastiCache and Aurora; messaging through SQS, EventBridge, SNS and SES; analytics with Athena over S3. The steps explain the rules that keep twenty-nine connecting lines from crossing.",
